---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import HmacGenerator from '../../components/HmacGenerator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="HMAC Generator" description="Generate an HMAC signature (SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-512) from a message and secret key, entirely in your browser.">
  <HmacGenerator client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>What HMAC is for</h2>
  <p>HMAC (Hash-based Message Authentication Code) verifies both the integrity and authenticity of a message — commonly used for webhook signature verification and API request signing.</p>

  <h2>Common HMAC Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Using a weak or short secret key</strong>, undermining the security HMAC is meant to provide.</li>
    <li><strong>Comparing HMAC output with a non-constant-time comparison</strong> in production code, which can theoretically leak timing information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This HMAC Generator</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Generating a signature to verify a webhook payload's authenticity</li>
    <li>Signing API requests to prove they came from an authorized client</li>
    <li>Testing HMAC verification logic during development</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
